{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Moshe and Aharon came.</b> This was not mentioned regarding the other plagues, that both of them came, for it is well known to all that Aharon was with him in all his affairs. The reason it is mentioned here is because it is about to say that both of them were driven out, as it is written: ״ויושב את משה ואת אהרן״ (and he sent back Moshe and Aharon)." "<b>To humble yourself before.</b> Because you exalt yourself over the rest of the survivors remaining to you from the hail." "<b>Thus said</b> etc. Many prophecies and commandments do not specify where HaShem said them — for example, the plague of locusts, and for example, ״כחצות הלילה״ (at midnight), and for example, ״שימו איש חרבו על ירכו״ (let each man place his sword on his thigh) of the calf, and for example, ״זאת חקת התורה״ (this is the statute of the Torah) in the section of the red heifer, and for example, ״זה הדבר אשר צוה ה׳״ (this is the matter that HaShem commanded) in the section of vows. And likewise many other prophets said many times ״כה אמר ה׳״ (thus said HaShem) without specifying where HaShem said them. Of this it is said: ״מקים דבר עבדו״ (who fulfills the word of His servant)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:54.685560065Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}